<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Azzan ibn Qais</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1871">1871</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Azzan ibn Qais was a member of the Al Bu Said family who, backed by the Ibadi religious leaders of the Omani interior, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscat">Muscat</a> in 1868 and was elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a>. His government tried to restore a strict Ibadi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imamate">imamate</a> on the coast, but it lacked British support and was overthrown by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Turki ibn Said, who defeated and killed him in 1871.</p></div>
